<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consult-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consult-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consult-table.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/">Free tools</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Scorecard</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Scorecard: An Insurance Appraisal Checklist</h1><p class="lede">Strong appraisals start with a complete file. Answer twelve quick questions to see where yours stands and what to fix before anyone signs a demand letter.</p></div></section><section class="sec sec-tool"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><p class="tool-title">Appraisal readiness scorecard</p><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to a Virginia attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Request the full line-item estimate, not just the summary page, in writing."><span>Do you have the insurer’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate. A lump-sum bid won’t hold up before a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather every photo you have and note when each was taken. Add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos of the damage taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ paragraph in the policy conditions and note any deadlines."><span>Have you read your policy’s appraisal clause?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Locate the ‘Suit Against Us’ clause and calendar the date. Our claim calendar builder can help."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Complete reasonable temporary repairs, such as tarps and water extraction, and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made and receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from your agent or insurer."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet walls, attics, crawlspaces and decking have been inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has all hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect emails, letters and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the insurer organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in our claim gap estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, return it before the deadline in the request."><span>If the insurer asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it submitted on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out score-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3e9f6" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#00297b" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div><p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Default figures are illustrative.</p><noscript><p class="tool-note">This calculator needs JavaScript. Everything runs in your browser and nothing is sent anywhere.</p></noscript></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the insurance appraisal checklist is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight. They decide whether appraisal is the right tool at all and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items matter too, but they’re easier to fix.</p>
<h2>What your score means</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and up:</strong> your file is in good shape. A professional review of the gap is the logical next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first. Each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are my answers saved or sent anywhere?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The scorecard runs in your browser and nothing is stored or transmitted.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share the result with an appraiser?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot of your score and to-do list and bring it to your consultation.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/fallen-tree-claim-splitter/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Fallen Tree Claim Splitter</span></a><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/claim-gap-and-fee-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Claim Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</span></a><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/holdback-recovery-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Holdback Recovery Calculator</span></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><p class="box-small">Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET · All of Virginia</p></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">All free tools</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/claim-gap-and-fee-estimator/">Claim Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/holdback-recovery-calculator/">Holdback Recovery Calculator</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/roof-pitch-and-squares-checker/">Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Checker</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/hurricane-wind-deductible-converter/">Hurricane &amp; Wind Deductible Converter</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/claim-clock-calendar-builder/">Claim Clock &amp; Calendar Builder</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/appraisal-readiness-scorecard/" aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Scorecard</a></li><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/fallen-tree-claim-splitter/">Fallen Tree Claim Splitter</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Want a professional to check the numbers?</h2><p>Send us your estimate and we’ll review it line by line.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
